---
import { site } from "../../data/site";
import { siteContainer } from "../layout/container";

const githubUsername =
  site.author.github.split("/").filter(Boolean).pop() ?? "LinCie";
const encodedGithubUsername = encodeURIComponent(githubUsername);
const githubProfile = site.author.github;
const githubStats = `https://github-profile-summary-cards.vercel.app/api/cards/stats?username=${encodedGithubUsername}&theme=default`;
const githubActivity = `https://ghchart.rshah.org/b8614b/${encodedGithubUsername}`;
const skillIcons =
  "https://skillicons.dev/icons?i=go,ts,nodejs,postgres,docker,redis,astro,tailwind&theme=light&perline=4";
---

<section
  class="border-b border-[#c4b49d] bg-[#fffdf8] py-14 md:py-20"
  aria-labelledby="profile-signals-title"
>
  <div class={siteContainer}>
    <div class="max-w-[70ch]">
      <p
        class="font-sans text-xs font-semibold tracking-[0.14em] text-[#843d2f] uppercase"
      >
        Small signals · a quieter dashboard
      </p>
      <h2
        id="profile-signals-title"
        class="mt-3 font-serif text-[clamp(1.8rem,3vw,2.6rem)] leading-[1.15] font-normal tracking-[-0.02em] text-[#2d332b]"
      >
        A few things moving through the station
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-base leading-[1.65] text-[#5f665c]">
        Profile widgets can turn a person into a scoreboard. These are gentler
        windows instead: a trail of open work, the tools I reach for, and a
        small note about what is keeping the room warm.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10 grid grid-cols-1 gap-6 lg:grid-cols-2">
      <article
        class="flex flex-col rounded-xl border border-[#c4b49d] bg-[#f7f2e8] p-6"
      >
        <div
          class="flex items-center justify-between gap-4 border-b border-[#c4b49d]/60 pb-3"
        >
          <div>
            <p
              class="font-sans text-xs font-semibold tracking-[0.06em] text-[#5f665c] uppercase"
            >
              Work trail · GitHub
            </p>
            <h3 class="mt-1 font-serif text-xl font-normal text-[#2d332b]">
              Open work leaves a trail.
            </h3>
          </div>
          <span
            class="grid size-9 shrink-0 place-items-center rounded-lg bg-[#e9ddc9] text-[#b8614b]"
            aria-hidden="true"
          >
            <svg
              class="size-5 fill-none [stroke:currentColor] [stroke-width:1.5] [stroke-linecap:round] [stroke-linejoin:round]"
              viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            >
              <path d="M12 3v18M3 12h18"></path>
              <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="8.5"></circle>
            </svg>
          </span>
        </div>

        <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-[1.65] text-[#5f665c]">
          Not a streak to maintain—just a living trace of experiments, fixes,
          and systems tended in public.
        </p>

        <figure class="mt-5 flex flex-1 flex-col justify-end">
          <a
            href={githubProfile}
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="block overflow-hidden rounded-lg border border-[#c4b49d]/70 bg-[#fffdf8] p-2 transition-[border-color,box-shadow] duration-200 hover:border-[#b8614b] hover:shadow-sm focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-[#b8614b] motion-reduce:transition-none"
            aria-label={`Open ${githubUsername}'s GitHub profile`}
          >
            <img
              src={githubStats}
              alt={`GitHub activity summary for ${githubUsername}`}
              width="340"
              height="200"
              loading="lazy"
              decoding="async"
              class="h-auto w-full"
            />
          </a>
          <figcaption class="mt-3 text-xs leading-[1.5] text-[#5f665c]">
            Public GitHub summary ·
            <a
              href={githubProfile}
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              class="font-semibold text-[#843d2f] underline decoration-[#b8614b] underline-offset-2 hover:text-[#b8614b]"
            >
              visit the profile
            </a>
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </article>

      <article
        class="flex flex-col rounded-xl border border-[#c4b49d] bg-[#f7f2e8] p-6"
      >
        <div
          class="flex items-center justify-between gap-4 border-b border-[#c4b49d]/60 pb-3"
        >
          <div>
            <p
              class="font-sans text-xs font-semibold tracking-[0.06em] text-[#5f665c] uppercase"
            >
              Tools on the bench
            </p>
            <h3 class="mt-1 font-serif text-xl font-normal text-[#2d332b]">
              Tools that fit my hands.
            </h3>
          </div>
          <span
            class="grid size-9 shrink-0 place-items-center rounded-lg bg-[#e9ddc9] text-[#b8614b]"
            aria-hidden="true"
          >
            <svg
              class="size-5 fill-none [stroke:currentColor] [stroke-width:1.5] [stroke-linecap:round] [stroke-linejoin:round]"
              viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            >
              <path
                d="m14.7 6.3 3 3M4 20l6.8-6.8M12.2 4.8a4 4 0 0 1 5.7 5.7L10 18.4 5.6 14z"
              ></path>
              <path d="m15.5 8.5-7 7"></path>
            </svg>
          </span>
        </div>

        <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-[1.65] text-[#5f665c]">
          A small technical snapshot, without pretending the tools are the whole
          story. I reach for Go and TypeScript, then let the data and the people
          decide what comes next.
        </p>

        <figure
          class="mt-5 rounded-lg border border-[#c4b49d]/70 bg-[#fffdf8] p-5"
        >
          <a
            href="https://skillicons.dev/"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="block rounded-md focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4 focus-visible:outline-[#b8614b]"
            aria-label="View the Skill Icons project"
          >
            <img
              src={skillIcons}
              alt="Icons for Go, TypeScript, Node.js, PostgreSQL, Docker, Redis, Astro, and Tailwind CSS"
              width="420"
              height="120"
              loading="lazy"
              decoding="async"
              class="mx-auto h-auto max-w-full"
            />
          </a>
          <figcaption
            class="mt-4 text-center text-xs leading-[1.5] text-[#5f665c]"
          >
            Go · TypeScript · Node.js · PostgreSQL · Docker · Redis · Astro ·
            Tailwind CSS
          </figcaption>
        </figure>

        <div class="mt-5 flex flex-wrap gap-2" aria-label="Selected tools">
          {
            ["Go", "TypeScript", "PostgreSQL", "Docker", "Astro"].map(
              (tool) => (
                <span class="rounded-full bg-[#e9ddc9] px-3 py-1 text-xs font-semibold text-[#2d332b]">
                  {tool}
                </span>
              ),
            )
          }
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>

    <article
      class="mt-6 rounded-xl border border-[#c4b49d] bg-[#f7f2e8] p-6 md:p-8"
    >
      <div
        class="flex flex-col justify-between gap-4 border-b border-[#c4b49d]/60 pb-4 sm:flex-row sm:items-end"
      >
        <div>
          <p
            class="font-sans text-xs font-semibold tracking-[0.06em] text-[#5f665c] uppercase"
          >
            The long view · contribution graph
          </p>
          <h3 class="mt-1 font-serif text-xl font-normal text-[#2d332b]">
            Small steps still count as a journey.
          </h3>
        </div>
        <a
          href={githubProfile}
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="inline-flex min-h-11 items-center text-xs font-bold text-[#843d2f] underline decoration-[#b8614b] underline-offset-4 hover:text-[#b8614b] focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4 focus-visible:outline-[#b8614b]"
        >
          See the source trail
        </a>
      </div>

      <p class="mt-4 max-w-[65ch] text-sm leading-[1.65] text-[#5f665c]">
        The graph is here as a landscape, not a leaderboard. It shows that
        patient, ordinary tending is part of the work too.
      </p>

      <figure
        class="mt-5 overflow-hidden rounded-lg border border-[#c4b49d]/70 bg-[#fffdf8] p-2"
      >
        <a
          href={githubProfile}
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="block rounded-md focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4 focus-visible:outline-[#b8614b]"
          aria-label={`Open ${githubUsername}'s GitHub contribution graph`}
        >
          <img
            src={githubActivity}
            alt={`GitHub contribution graph for ${githubUsername}`}
            width="663"
            height="104"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
            class="h-auto w-full"
          />
        </a>
        <figcaption class="px-2 pt-3 pb-1 text-xs leading-[1.5] text-[#5f665c]">
          Activity graph generated from public GitHub data. It may be quiet on
          some days; quiet does not mean empty.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </article>

    <aside
      class="mt-6 grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 rounded-xl border border-[#c4b49d] bg-[#e9ddc9] p-6 sm:grid-cols-3"
      aria-label="Current personal signals"
    >
      <div>
        <p
          class="font-sans text-xs font-semibold tracking-[0.08em] text-[#843d2f] uppercase"
        >
          Making
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 font-serif text-lg text-[#2d332b]">
          Backend systems that stay understandable.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p
          class="font-sans text-xs font-semibold tracking-[0.08em] text-[#843d2f] uppercase"
        >
          Returning to
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 font-serif text-lg text-[#2d332b]">
          Technical care is still care.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p
          class="font-sans text-xs font-semibold tracking-[0.08em] text-[#843d2f] uppercase"
        >
          Enjoying
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 font-serif text-lg text-[#2d332b]">
          Warm light, quiet stations, and Stardew Valley.
        </p>
      </div>
    </aside>

    <p class="mt-5 text-xs leading-[1.55] text-[#5f665c]">
      The live cards come from public GitHub data and may be unavailable or
      cached. The written notes above remain the complete version of the story.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
